{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20287",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.17,
      "end_seconds": 4.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.0,
      "end_seconds": 11.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "Right, yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.19,
      "end_seconds": 21.2,
      "duration_seconds": 8.01,
      "text": "I wanted to get sharp pain in the upper right of my tummy looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.24,
      "end_seconds": 29.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.45,
      "end_seconds": 40.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.49,
      "end_seconds": 65.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 99 percent, pressure 117 over 81. And heart rate 79, temp 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.4,
      "end_seconds": 69.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.76,
      "end_seconds": 73.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "We'll look at it together shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.99,
      "end_seconds": 92.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.16,
      "end_seconds": 95.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "For two weeks, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.04,
      "end_seconds": 106.42,
      "duration_seconds": 9.38,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.37,
      "end_seconds": 116.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.68,
      "text": "Honestly, once or twice a day. Yes, fatty meals. That makes it worse. Severe, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.21,
      "end_seconds": 129.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "And what about fever or dark urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.69,
      "end_seconds": 133.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "No, no fever or dark urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.75,
      "end_seconds": 137.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "How about pale stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.13,
      "end_seconds": 141.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, no pale stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.54,
      "end_seconds": 146.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Alright, on the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.87,
      "end_seconds": 150.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.45,
      "end_seconds": 158.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Okay, are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.3,
      "end_seconds": 165.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Yes, tramadol, it gives me feeling very drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.11,
      "end_seconds": 186.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.71,
      "end_seconds": 198.78,
      "duration_seconds": 11.07,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days. I'm vegetarian and have been for years. My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.36,
      "end_seconds": 201.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.56,
      "end_seconds": 204.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.17,
      "end_seconds": 214.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.03,
      "end_seconds": 217.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "No, no conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.63,
      "end_seconds": 221.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Any regular medication at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.56,
      "end_seconds": 226.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "No, I'm not on anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.93,
      "end_seconds": 232.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.8,
      "end_seconds": 236.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.45,
      "end_seconds": 259.14,
      "duration_seconds": 7.69,
      "text": "There is tenderness under the right ribs when you breathe in, and no yellowing of the eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.13,
      "end_seconds": 268.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.91,
      "end_seconds": 283.21,
      "duration_seconds": 9.3,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Having listened and examined, I think we're dealing with biliary colic from gallstones at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.03,
      "end_seconds": 286.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.65,
      "end_seconds": 310.6,
      "duration_seconds": 21.95,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now biliary colic from gallstones is my leading thought, not anything worse. We should do an ultrasound of the tummy for right upper quadrant pain. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.54,
      "end_seconds": 314.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Okay, I'll do it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.56,
      "end_seconds": 347.07,
      "duration_seconds": 31.51,
      "text": "I'd like you to take diclofenac, 50 milligrams, three times a day if needed, for three days. You take it by mouth. It's for gallbladder pain. Keep meals small and low in fat until we have the scan. I'll also refer you to the surgeons. Do get help quickly if you develop a fever, yellow eyes or severe constant pain. Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.05,
      "end_seconds": 357.27,
      "duration_seconds": 9.22,
      "text": "So, I take the diclofenac, 50 milligrams, three times a day if needed. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.73,
      "end_seconds": 364.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.36,
      "end_seconds": 368.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.92,
      "end_seconds": 371.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}